# The first window played with real input: a click and a drag with the mouse, Alt+Tab, typing and Alt+F4 with the keyboard, and a click on a close box. The steps before the first frame are the first window's set-up, which a live session performs itself; the first frame is its first mark.
desk-scenario 1
screen 640 480
depths 8 4
open notes 60 60 300 180 "Notes"
label notes 12 12 "The first window."
open welcome 220 150 340 200 "Welcome to Desk"
label welcome 12 12 "Type something:"
field welcome 12 36 300
pointer 320 240
frame start
# A click on Notes' title bar focuses and raises it.
pointer 120 70
press left
release left
frame focus
# A drag of its title bar by (40, 30), in two moves.
press left
move 20 15
move 20 15
release left
frame dragged
# Alt+Tab picks Welcome on release.
key LeftAlt down
key Tab down
key Tab up
key LeftAlt up
frame switched
# Welcome's field takes the typing.
type "live"
frame typed
# Alt+F4 closes Welcome and focuses Notes.
key LeftAlt down
key F4 down
key F4 up
key LeftAlt up
frame closed
# A click on Notes' close box (it is now at (100, 90), so the box is at x 374..392, y 92..110) leaves the empty desktop. The pointer goes
# straight across (no vertical move), because DOSBox's mouse driver holds back a one-pixel move until the next one.
pointer 383 100
press left
release left
frame clicked
# One more move, so the cursor is not where it started.
move 50 60
frame move
